# Purl

**Save the links worth keeping. Share the ones worth passing on.**

Purl is a calm place to save and share the links you find — a home for your "pearls". Users save URLs (web pages, PDFs, YouTube videos, audio); Purl resolves each link's metadata (title, favicon, description, thumbnail) and keeps them in one place, organized in folders. Any folder can be made public and shared at `/@username/slug`.

There is no AI layer: the old in-app chat and the extraction/embeddings/semantic-search pipeline were removed.

Every account is free, with one limit: 1,000 saved links. Purl is also available through a REST API (`/api/v1`) and an MCP server (`/api/mcp`).

For architecture, commands, conventions and gotchas, read `CLAUDE.md` at the repository root; it is the source of truth.
